      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "The entity update and operation queue\ninsertion should be part of same\nIndexedDB transaction",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "The entity update and operation queue insertion should be part of same IndexedDB transaction",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "x4_72J-5et93_khUczbnl",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -286.919135979987,
      "y": -647.3225989619059,
      "width": 726.5958612479578,
      "height": 30.594041443273795,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "ax",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1185137857,
      "version": 87,
      "versionNonce": 1484718497,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1791559280689,
      "created": 1791559167640,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "*** STORAGE ARCHITECTURE *** (IndexedDB vs others)",
      "fontSize": 24.475233154619037,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "*** STORAGE ARCHITECTURE *** (IndexedDB vs others)",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "u9B-Etlqr_1hhjpfKsc__",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -281.1616731012915,
      "y": -609.6036745786613,
      "width": 926.7811367282316,
      "height": 963.6599452352145,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "ay",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1686351311,
      "version": 1225,
      "versionNonce": 912664335,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1791559578575,
      "created": 1791559202263,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1) React storage (memory only with limited capacity) --> best for active UI\nstate\n\n2) localStorage (persistent and synchronous with small capacity, complicated to\nparse) --> preferences or simple flags\n\n3) IndexedDB (persistent and synchronous, with browser-dependent capacity) \n--> structured offline application data\n\n4) Cache storage (persistent, browser dependent capacity) --> use for network\nresponse and app assets\n\n5) OPFS (WebAPI - original private file systems) - persistent and browser\ndependent --> used for large binary files and specialized storages ==> faster\nthan indexedDB\n\n* main thread, it uses asynchronous Promise APIs\n(navigator.storage.getDirectory(), Blob, WritableFileStream).\n* Web Worker, it supports high-speed synchronous file access via\ncreateSyncAccessHandle() (getSize, write, read, truncate, flush, close).\n\n6) Service worker (not DB, execution layer) --> used for offline request\ninterception and caching\n\n* A Service Worker should not be treated as an always-running process.\nBrowsers can terminate it when idle.\n* browser storage is not an unconditional durability guarantee. Users can clear\nsite data, browsers can evict best-effort storage, and private browsing\nenvironments may impose restrictions.\n* Request persistent storage using navigator.storage.persist() when appropriate,\nwhile retaining recovery pa\n\n",
      "fontSize": 23.36145321782338,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1) React storage (memory only with limited capacity) --> best for active UI state\n\n2) localStorage (persistent and synchronous with small capacity, complicated to parse) --> preferences or simple flags\n\n3) IndexedDB (persistent and synchronous, with browser-dependent capacity) \n--> structured offline application data\n\n4) Cache storage (persistent, browser dependent capacity) --> use for network response and app assets\n\n5) OPFS (WebAPI - original private file systems) - persistent and browser dependent --> used for large binary files and specialized storages ==> faster than indexedDB\n\n* main thread, it uses asynchronous Promise APIs (navigator.storage.getDirectory(), Blob, WritableFileStream).\n* Web Worker, it supports high-speed synchronous file access via createSyncAccessHandle() (getSize, write, read, truncate, flush, close).\n\n6) Service worker (not DB, execution layer) --> used for offline request interception and caching\n\n* A Service Worker should not be treated as an always-running process. Browsers can terminate it when idle.\n* browser storage is not an unconditional durability guarantee. Users can clear site data, browsers can evict best-effort storage, and private browsing environments may impose restrictions.\n* Request persistent storage using navigator.storage.persist() when appropriate, while retaining recovery pa\n\n",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "gygRDd33hVNhQXNX4grV-",
