    {
      "id": "0m6Dq9XVgU0ON_cYmXbNH",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -318.2917575241656,
      "y": 4330.029456572152,
      "width": 800,
      "height": 250,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0y",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1788398785,
      "version": 4,
      "versionNonce": 552071407,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1791563696252,
      "created": 1791563689658,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "• Operational Transformation (OT): A transform-first approach that treats\nedits as a sequence of operations. When concurrent edits happen, a central\nserver adjusts or transforms incoming operations relative to other concurrent\nactions so that every client arrives at the exact same output.\n\n• Conflict-free Replicated Data Types (CRDTs): A decentralized approach that\nembeds merge logic directly into the data structure. Operations or states are\nmathematically commutative, associative, and idempotent, meaning replicas can\nreceive updates in any order and still converge automatically without needing a\ncentral coordinator.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "• Operational Transformation (OT): A transform-first approach that treats edits as a sequence of operations. When concurrent edits happen, a central server adjusts or transforms incoming operations relative to other concurrent actions so that every client arrives at the exact same output.\n\n• Conflict-free Replicated Data Types (CRDTs): A decentralized approach that embeds merge logic directly into the data structure. Operations or states are mathematically commutative, associative, and idempotent, meaning replicas can receive updates in any order and still converge automatically without needing a central coordinator.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "zf_9406VuGiYWkjNYvq7_",
      "type": "text",
